#edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410102} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cfb75b6-b8ba-5513-85da-49f6a4546360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410066} {:answer/id #uuid "d57eea81-3aed-50fc-b8cb-ac92bc70c961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cfb75b6-b8ba-5513-85da-49f6a4546360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410066} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee6c6021-4135-5e83-9510-560eaf4934a5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410104}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "594bcd16-11e5-554c-954b-51c8f4ae33f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-182392" :question/problem "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∧B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "First, we add a column for $A∧B.$ Remember that $A∧B$ is true if both $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A∧B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nThen, we add a column for $¬(A∧B).$ Remember that the truth values of $¬(A∧B)$ are opposite those of $A∧B.$\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A∧B\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∧B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375446 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152054 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69612c9a-699f-5635-8c9c-649a93ab4583" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Double Negation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00092e11-dfc2-522f-b7e7-9f9a2f677aba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∧B)∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375448} {:answer/id #uuid "6bb0eafe-3c5e-5119-81d5-fd4d25a57bcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(¬A∧¬B)∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375449} {:answer/id #uuid "b38ed039-9158-54ee-a5db-ae6ef7808e73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(¬A∧B)∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375450} {:answer/id #uuid "aaf4b998-6316-553f-9a44-6fbc091351e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬(A∧B)∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375451} {:answer/id #uuid "29401c33-69b4-5f44-8675-be05f2e42e0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∧¬B)∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00092e11-dfc2-522f-b7e7-9f9a2f677aba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(A∧B)∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375448} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6aecff2-024b-5ca3-9318-2f115c576eb6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375447}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "eb55c8f8-ed83-5b11-8c56-ffc107c88f23" :question/math-academy-id "q-81365" :question/problem "Simplify the statement $¬[¬(A∧¬(¬B))]∨B.$" :question/worked-solution "Two negations in a row cancel each other out. So, we can simplify $¬(¬B)$ to $B.$ \n\nAs a result of this, the statement simplifes to \n\n$$\n¬(¬(A∧B))∨B.\n$$\n\nThen, we can simplify $¬(¬(A∧B))$ to $A∧B.$\n\nTherefore, the given statement can be simplified to \n\n$$\n(A∧B)∨B.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410106 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152052 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93415651-fbcb-56d3-ad93-2b7f34e7bf4c" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Negated Sentence in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cf34be5-c594-5496-aa61-41f145440bc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬P∨¬Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410072} {:answer/id #uuid "7371329d-96b6-51ea-bfe7-14de7b40abf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬(P∧Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410077} {:answer/id #uuid "964b4c56-2ede-5a41-8d97-6bcfd3830f9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬P∧Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410082} {:answer/id #uuid "9beb2485-dd7e-565f-bf11-7179015d4947" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬(P∨Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410083} {:answer/id #uuid "cd5a65eb-c2e8-56a1-b5c7-79f43616d6f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬P∨Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410088}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9beb2485-dd7e-565f-bf11-7179015d4947" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬(P∨Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410083} :answer-field/id #uuid "81e17c23-e75b-5224-95d3-5b0d550456c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bc8abf72-5929-5991-bf8d-19db968b0381" :question/math-academy-id "q-81400" :question/problem "$10$ is **not** divisible by $3$ or $4.$\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following:\n\n- $P:10\\text{ is divisible by }3$\n\n- $Q:10\\text{ is divisible by }4$" :question/worked-solution "The given sentence is the negation of the following sentence: \n\n$10$ is divisible by $3$ or $4$, \n\nwhich can be expressed symbolically as $P∨Q.$\n\nThe negation is represented by the symbol \"$¬$\". \n\nTherefore, the given sentence is expressed symbolically as $¬(P∨Q).$"}]}
